+ "status_superseded_rev4b": "gnc.json v3.1 (2026-10-13): built as rev2.2 from rev2.1 (c2860bd89c1e5920) with the corrections C1-C5 of the independent document check REV-GNC-4 (lead lines 189, 190); published by the lead. Simulation and analysis evidence only; nothing here is physical approval. VALIDITY (REV-GNC-4 C2, lead line 190): every P, reserve, propellant-closure and apogee-trim figure in this document was computed at GNC mass ledger v3d (18 items, total 13.6706 kg); CAD v3.5 is +0.87 to +1.17 kg heavier (valve pair at its 2 x 0.15 kg target / at the ASSUMED 0.60 kg; REV-GNC-4 (f)), far beyond the 0.10 kg re-fly trigger (181 (5)), so the 285 m target and its P are NOT demonstrated for the current design until the rev3 flights at the v3.5.1 ledger (rev3 P2). Decided state for GNC: (1) A1 apogee target 285 m ADOPTED with conditions (175 (1), 181 (6)): the launch-commit wind rule W10 < 6 m/s AND sigma_u(3 m) <= 1.0 m/s is HARD for A1 and now also carries the R2 flame-out margin (186 (2)); 285 m coverage on all four bases and on pl, e19, the prep path, L400 and PURGE NOT RUN is rev3 P3. (2) Mass change control (181 (5)): re-fly at the actual ledger for any confirmed landing-mass growth >= 0.10 kg over ledger v3d; a 0.20 kg hardware allowance counts against that trigger until fasteners and seals are in the BOM (188 (11)); the v3.5 / v3.5.1 flights are rev3 P2. (3) FC_THRUST NOT armed on A1 (168 (5), 175 (6), 181 (3)); RG-16 is budgeted at the detector output; PROVISIONAL detection-latency allowance 0.5 s from the onset of the 670 N plateau, strict windowed form, no window-gain credit (REVIEWER 2.973 % against the allowed 2.985 %: 0.012 percentage points of margin, relative 0.4 %, on an ASSUMED white vibration model; not robust); the trajectory consequence of 0.5 s at 670 N, the B1 miss side and the non-white sensitivity are rev3 P5. (4) Late purge commit (181 (2) as amended by 186 (1)): L* = 1.3 s for both the LO and the HI bracket; PURGE commits iff the lead from the commit to the plain relight trigger is >= 1.3 s; below it there is no purge and no unpurged relight on that pass (drogue descent; vehicle loss in the FMEA). The earlier 1.7 s value of 181 (2) and its premise (an unpurged LO start at P_total ~0.75) are REFUTED and replaced: at the worst PURGE NOT RUN states an unpurged start succeeds with P 0 under LO and under HI (light, release at E2, vapour gap, A3: a dead vehicle released at about -32 m/s; 186 (1)). The alternative, an unpurged relight with the drogue release held to >= E2 + 0.22 s, is flown in rev3 P6 and is adopted only if it gains P without the released-dead-vehicle hazard; LO/HI stays open (CF-4 generation runs, T4). 'The 0.81 s plan holds' is scoped to the predictor path. (5) Drogue release with Pc invalid (181 (4), 186 (2)): R2 ADOPTED in design over R1, pcf_tmax 0.5 s; R2 COMMAND HOLD ADOPTED: while the drogue is attached with Pc invalid, the ECU open-loop command is held at the start level 62.5 N until the release. Reason: Combustion v2.4a DERIVED adiabatic bound of the cold-flow apparent thrust after an undetected flame-out with Pc invalid (open-loop lift; 02-combustion/data/v2p4a/cold_flow_thrust_v2p4a.csv (e094c4be80d12f66)): 12.5-13.3 N at the 62.5 N start level, 35.6-37.5 N at a 200 N command (lead lines 185, 186 (2)); at the start level the bound consumes the all-winds R2 margin (4.16 N) and stays inside the W10 < 6 m/s margin (16.31 N) unless chamber heat pick-up is large (TO-VERIFY: CF-3 with a load cell, a post-burn N2O pulse in the T series). R2 v2 with F_cold(lift, P_tank) in the flame-out case is rev3 P4. (6) The k_hat / apex freeze on Pc invalid is REFUTED and withdrawn (175 (4)); its replacement (re-reference to throttle-map thrust) is rev3 P7; Pc VALID is a launch-commit condition. (7) A1 FMEA inputs (fmea_inputs_rev2p1): no over-thrust detector after an in-flight Pc loss (181 (3)); a pass below L* is a vehicle loss (186 (1)); 'R2 holds the drogue' after an undetected flame-out depends