+    "text": "(a) Counting start and flush, as implemented in sim6 V2 (gnc_dev6/7): E2 = the 6-DOF light (rel_dt 0); Pc is invalid from E2 + pcf_dt (pcf_dt 0 in the decided set). Counting starts on the first 1 ms step at which both hold and the 100 Hz frames are then taken every 10 ms from that step (frame phase tied to the counting start, not to a free-running FC clock: TO-VERIFY against the flight FC). Mode 3 (the R2 v2 candidate): the axial specific force is filtered continuously (first order, fct_tau 20 ms) from the drogue phase and is NOT flushed at E2 or at the Pc-invalid onset; the reference and the descent rate are sampled at E2 and the drag term is compensated by (vz/vz(E2))^2. Release needs 3 consecutive frames >= 37.16 N (3-frame running minimum) and the engine lit; not confirmed by E2 + pcf_tmax -> abort (hold). Consequence: lit thrust before a later flame-out stays in the filter for about 3 tau = 60 ms, so a vehicle that lights and dies 10-20 ms after E2 can meet the 3-frame rule on carried-over thrust; GNC's flown flame-out population is the never-lit cold-flow design bound with onsets 0 / 5 / 10 ms and does not contain this case. The sim also gates release on the engine-lit truth (ECU RUN), which a real ECU without valid Pc cannot know; GNC's 'released dead vehicle' counts are therefore computed from the window statistics, not from flown releases. ADOPTED as a flight-software requirement (lead 227 (6), the first option of the rev4 proposal): the mode-3 filter is re-initialised at the Pc-invalid onset; Electronics implements it in v2.11 and runs S17 (onsets 1-50 ms x frame phases x noise); GNC re-runs the R2 v2 statistics with the flush afterwards (the alternative, counting from onset + 3 tau, is not adopted). (b) The 20.85 N W10 < 6 bound is the largest sim R2 estimate over the W10 < 6 flame-out runs (R2 v1, rev2, 0.5 s; the v3.1 margin 16.31 N = 37.16 - 20.85 N). It contains the modelled ADIS16470 white noise (100 ug/rtHz ASSUMED, about 0.06 N rms on the estimate after the 20 ms filter at ~16 kg, DERIVED) and the bias / scale / mass-estimate dispersions. It does NOT contain an FC frame noise of 5 N rms (about 90 x the modelled level), drogue canopy breathing (quasi-steady massless drogue), FC timing jitter, or structural vibration of an unlit vehicle (the sim's vibration term scales with thrust). Frame noise (DERIVED; REV-GNC-6 Monte Carlo under these assumptions, RV6-07): 5 N rms frame noise (iid ASSUMED) raises the window maximum of the 3-frame minimum by +3.1 N median / +7.8 N p99 over 50 frames (0.5 s) and +3.8 / +8.2 N over 80 frames (0.8 s). Against the R2 v2 mode-3 margins at W10 < 6 (+5.98 N at 0.5 s, +5.30 N at 0.8 s) the bounding run would be released with probability 6.5 % / 18.4 %; against the v3.1 R2 margin (16.31 N = 37.16 - 20.85 N) the probability is about 0. LEAD (227 (6)): Electronics states the FC frame-noise budget against the +5.3 to +6.0 N mode-3 margin; the 'no released dead vehicle' claim is used only with that budget. (c) Starve threshold (rev4, item [6]): 0.30 s at the 0.5 s window (all lit runs released; 5/60 aborted at 0.40 s), 0.60 s at the 0.8 s window (W10 < 6: 0.65 s). (SIM, N=60, A1_none pw, 285 m v3d trim; transfer to 210 m / v3.5.1 ASSUMED; 0/60 aborts gives a one-sided 95 % UB of 4.9 %). With the 0.8 s window every lit run is released up to 0.60 s, but landings fall with the plateau (all winds 58/60 at 0.40 s, 55 at 0.45-0.50 s, 50/60 at 0.60 s; W10 < 6 44/44 to 0.55 s, 43/44 at 0.60 s); with 0.5 s at 0.40 s 53 of 55 released land. The window choice decides release; the starve itself costs landings. GNC's R2 v2 releases 0.08-0.12 s after the plateau ends, about 0.1 s later than Electronics' stand-in (0.46-0.48 s at 0.5 s), so the 0.5 s window has no margin over the top of the 0.1-0.4 s starve range and the 0.8 s window has >= 0.20 s. The ECU backstop (line 216 (2)(b): the hold ends by E2 + 0.8 s + margin) is compatible: GNC's latest release at the 0.8 s window is E2 + 0.80 s (st_T 0.6-0.7 s), so the R2 v2 decision precedes the backstop by the stated margin (>= 2 FC frames + link latency, Electronics). LEAD (227 (5)): 0.8 s ADOPTED for the W10 < 6 m/s launch-commit envelope (scope RV6-08); Electronics v2.11 carries 0.8 s into its S17 sweep and confirms it or returns it to the lead.",
